<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Stable-only ruleset for versions-maven-plugin.

    Without this, every `versions:display-*` sweep re-proposes the same
    pre-release candidates that have already been rejected by name in
    docs/dependency-upgrade-log.md — log4j 3.0.0-beta*, slf4j 2.1.0-alpha1,
    the six maven-* 4.0.0-beta-*, maven-site 4.0.0-M16, the jakarta *-M* APIs,
    httpclient5 5.7-alpha1, httpcore5 5.5-beta2, micrometer 1.18.0-M1.
    That noise is how a rejected alpha eventually gets merged by reflex.

    Matching is whole-string (Pattern.matches), so a trailing qualifier only
    matches when it ends the version. That is what keeps legitimate stable
    releases visible: 20260922.1 (date-versioned), 33.7.1-jre, 1.10.29, and
    v3-rev20260901-2.0.0 all fail the pattern.

    ONE CONSEQUENCE, deliberate: commons-fileupload2 is itself on a milestone
    line (2.0.0-M5), so intermediate M6/M7 bumps are now hidden. That is the
    wanted behaviour — the M4 -> M5 bump was a breaking API change
    (setFileSizeMax(int) removed, AttachmentServlet), so this line is pinned by
    judgement, not by lag. Its eventual GA still surfaces: Maven orders
    2.0.0-M5 < 2.0.0, so the stable release is reported as an update.

    Per-artifact <rule> ignoreVersions ADD to this global set, they cannot
    subtract from it — so do not try to re-enable a qualifier for one artifact
    here. Check that artifact manually instead.

    Usage: wired as <rulesUri> in the root pom's pluginManagement, so both the
    CLI goals and the reporting run pick it up. To deliberately see
    pre-releases again for one sweep:
        mvn versions:display-dependency-updates -Dmaven.version.rules=
-->
<ruleset comparisonMethod="maven"
         xmlns="http://www.mojohaus.org/versions-maven-plugin/rule/2.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.mojohaus.org/versions-maven-plugin/rule/2.0.0
                             https://www.mojohaus.org/versions-maven-plugin/xsd/rule-2.0.0.xsd">

  <ignoreVersions>
    <!-- alpha | beta | milestone | preview | snapshot | pre | rc | cr | ea | dev | m,
         each optionally followed by a separator and a build number.
         'preview' precedes 'pre' and 'milestone' precedes 'm' so the longer
         token wins the alternation. -->
    <ignoreVersion type="regex">(?i).*[-_.](alpha|beta|milestone|preview|snapshot|pre|rc|cr|ea|dev|m)[-_.]?\d*</ignoreVersion>
  </ignoreVersions>

</ruleset>
